  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be the point on the parabola, <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi></math> which is at a minimum distance from the center&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> of the circle&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.&nbsp;Then the equation of the circle, passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> and having its center at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
